cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Situational Safety for Embodied Agents
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singal
    given-names: Akanksha
repository-code: "https://github.com/AkankshaSingal8/situational_safety_for_embodied_agents"
abstract: >-
  A VLM-grounded safety filter for vision-language-action policies in tabletop
  manipulation. Semantic safety predicates proposed by a VLM are grounded into
  parametric spatial constraints, assembled into control barrier functions, and
  used to filter a policy's nominal action through a CBF-QP at each timestep.
  Evaluated on SafeLIBERO and LIBERO-Safety.
license: MIT
